questions.question:
A reviewer suggests dropping the script and doing the check in TypeScript, because "every Redis command is atomic anyway":

const stored = Number(await redis.hget("lb:ver", u.learnerId) ?? 0);
if (u.version > stored) {
  await redis.zadd("lb:all", u.totalScore, u.learnerId);
  await redis.hset("lb:ver", u.learnerId, String(u.version));
}

Timeline with two consumer workers (u_2290, stored version 14, total 340):

t1 worker A  HGET lb:ver u_2290 -> "14"   (A holds v16, total 410)
t2 worker B  HGET lb:ver u_2290 -> "14"   (B holds v15, total 380)
t3 worker A  ZADD lb:all 410 u_2290; HSET lb:ver u_2290 16
t4 worker B  ZADD lb:all 380 u_2290; HSET lb:ver u_2290 15

Statement: "Because each of HGET, ZADD and HSET is atomic, this version of the code cannot end with an older total on the board."
